      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 edit chain\n\nGenerate, then edit, then edit again \u2014 each stage takes the previous result as `input_image`, so you refine one image a step at a time and only pay for the step you changed.\n\nEach stage is a group. ComfyUI only re-runs a node whose inputs changed, and every FLUX 3 node here has a **fixed** `variation`, so editing **Edit 2**'s text re-runs Edit 2 alone; stages 1 and Edit 1 come from cache for free. Bump a stage's `variation` to re-roll just that stage (and everything after it).\n\n**Fast Groups Bypasser** (rgthree) toggles the edit stages. A bypassed stage makes no call and hands its input image straight on, so the chain always ends at the last active stage: bypass both edits while you settle the base image, or bypass just Edit 1 to apply Edit 2 to the base directly. Bypass rather than mute \u2014 a muted Edit 1 would leave Edit 2 with no image, and it would quietly run as text-to-image.\n\nThe base prompt is the **Shared Prompt**; each edit's instruction is a core **Text (Multiline)** node, so the instructions sit in plain view beside the stage they drive. `resolution` on the edits is **match_input**, so the size never drifts across the chain.\n\n**Image Comparer** shows base vs final; each stage also has a preview so you can see where a change crept in.\n\n### Needs\n[rgthree-comfy](https://github.com/rgthree/rgthree-comfy). **Manager \u2192 Install Missing Custom Nodes** finds it if the graph loads with red nodes.\n\n## The prompt lives in one node\n\nThe **Shared Prompt** node feeds every FLUX 3 `prompt` in this graph, so there is one\nplace to edit it. It emits a plain string, **not** a list, so each node it feeds still runs once."
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
